    {
      "id": "prompt_1",
      "provider": "prompt",
      "config": {
        "instructions": [
          "You are a lease audit analyst. You will receive a lease summary and an operating expense bill. Your task is to compare each bill line item against the lease's allowed/excluded expense rules and produce a structured finding.",
          "",
          "LEASE RULES (from lease summary):",
          "- Tenant pays 15% of Building Operating Expenses (Clause 4.1)",
          "- INCLUDED expenses (Clause 4.2): real estate taxes, insurance, common area utilities, janitorial, security, landscaping, HVAC maintenance, elevator maintenance, property management fees (capped at 4%), common area capital improvements (amortized)",
          "- EXCLUDED expenses (Clause 4.3): capital expenditures for structural repairs (roof, foundation, load-bearing walls), landlord legal fees unrelated to building operations, marketing/leasing commissions, depreciation, costs to cure landlord defaults, penalties/fines, environmental remediation pre-lease, landlord overhead/admin salaries not building-related, costs for services not provided, expenses for other tenant spaces not benefiting this tenant",
          "- Audit rights: 180 days from annual statement (Clause 4.4)",
          "- Gross-up at 80% occupancy if below (Clause 4.5)",
          "",
          "For each bill, produce ONE finding with these exact fields:",
          "1. bill_name (string): e.g., \"Westside Centre - May 2026\"",
          "2. status (enum): \"safe\" | \"needs_review\" | \"likely_overcharge\"",
          "3. reason (string): plain-language explanation",
          "4. evidence (string): exact lease/bill excerpts used, e.g., \"Lease Clause 4.3; bill lines 11-14\"",
          "5. amount_at_risk (string): e.g., \"$1,240\" (total excluded amounts × 15%)",
          "6. confidence (number 0-100 or \"low\"/\"medium\"/\"high\")",
          "",
          "HARD SAFETY RULES:",
          "- If any required field cannot be determined → status \"needs_review\" with reason describing what's missing",
          "- NEVER invent a clause, amount, or legal conclusion",
          "- When in doubt, downgrade to needs_review rather than guess",
          "- Only flag \"likely_overcharge\" when bill clearly contains excluded expense categories with identifiable amounts",
          "- \"safe\" only when all bill items map to allowed categories in Clause 4.2"
        ],
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "input": [
        {
          "lane": "text",
          "from": "parse_1"
        },
        {
          "lane": "questions",
          "from": "parse_1"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 460,
          "y": 200
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 66
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "llm_anthropic_1",
      "provider": "llm_anthropic",
      "config": {
        "profile": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
        "claude-sonnet-4-6": {
          "apikey": "${ROCKETRIDE_ANTHROPIC_KEY}"
        },
        "parameters": {}
      },
      "control": [
        {
          "classType": "llm",
          "from": "prompt_1"
        }
      ],
      "ui": {
        "position": {
          "x": 460,
          "y": 360
        },
        "measured": {
          "width": 150,
          "height": 66
        },
        "nodeType": "default",
        "formDataValid": true
      }
    },
    {
